# Easy Grade

Desktop app that grades student projects (Colab notebook + video walkthrough) against a rubric.
The professor opens a folder of submissions; everything runs locally.

## Architecture
- `grader/` is the engine (rubric, SQLite store, import, scoring contract, export). It must not import pywebview.
- `desktop/api.py` is the only bridge to the screen. Each public method of `Api` is callable from JS as
  `window.pywebview.api.<name>(...)` and returns `{"ok": True, ...}` or `{"ok": False, "error": "..."}`.
  Wrap new methods with `@_safe`. Methods/attributes starting with `_` are not exposed to JS.
- Open a new `GradeStore` per call (`with self._store() as st:`); SQLite connections can't cross threads.
- The app only writes inside `<folder>/_grading/`.
- `ui/index.html` is plain HTML/CSS/JS, no build step, no CDN (must work offline). Escape all
  student-provided text with `esc()`. Never insert notebook HTML outputs.
- When you add an `Api` method, add the same method to `ui/dev_mock.js` and a test in `tests/`.
- AI scores must go through `parse_grader_output` (scores limited to rubric levels). AI only drafts;
  the professor approves.
- AI calls live in `grader/ai_grader.py` (plain urllib, Anthropic Messages API, forced `submit_grades` tool).
  Tests must use a fake `post` function: never call the real API or need a key in tests.
- The API key lives only in `desktop/settings.py`'s per-user settings file or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Never log it,
  never write it in the repo or `_grading/`.

## Rules
- Never commit real student files, `_grading/`, `*.db`, or exports. The repo is public.
- Run `python -m unittest discover tests` after changes; all tests must pass.
- Error messages are shown to the professor verbatim: say what went wrong and how to fix it.
